sec.p:
Integration with PDWA: The distance-weighted attention mechanism in Algorithm 1 operates on these sub-matrices, applying the computed distance weights αij to adjust attention as Hij′=αij×Hij.
Algorithm 1 Path Distance-Weighted Attention (PDWA).
Require: Document paths P={p1,p2,…,pN}, target relation rht, entity representations E
Ensure: Enhanced relation representations {rhi,ti}i=1N 1:
Step 1: Path-to-Relation Mapping 2:
for each document path pi∈P do 3:
Extract sentence embeddings si from path pi 4:
si←Attention(rht,si,si) ▹ Attention with relation as query 5:
si←GumbelSoftmax(Linear(si)) ▹ Select most relevant sentence 6:
end for 7:
Step 2: Distance Matrix Computation 8:
for each pair (pi,pj) where i,j∈{1,2,…,N} do 9:
Dis(i,j)←1DotProductSimilarity(si,sj) ▹ Compute semantic distance10:
αi,j←Dis(i,j)∑k=1N|Dis(i,k)|2 ▹ Normalize distance weights11:
end for12:
Step 3: Attention Matrix Adjustment13:
Divide original relation matrix M into N×N sub-matrices {Mij}14:
for each sub-matrix Mij do15:
Hij←Attention(Mij) ▹ Compute attention for sub-matrix16:
Hij′←αij×Hij ▹ Apply distance weighting17:
end for18:
Step 4: Relation Representation Generation19:
for each path pi do20:
rhi,ti←ExtractTargetRelation(M^′(l),pi) ▹ Extract from final layer21:
end for22:
return {rhi,ti}i=1N
